# Where the keepers stand.
#
# The engine fills a board depth-first down lane 0, so a party of three arrives in single file:
# leader at (0,0), the two keepers behind it at (0,1) and (0,2). A hold is three abreast on the
# front rank, and this verb is the game's one word for it, so that the tests and anything else
# that wants to set a line up say the same thing.
#
# The host does not call it. `runtime.Place(who, lane, rank)` is the same move from C# -- it
# raises `moved`, a `before_moved` listener can refuse it, and a place the board does not have is
# refused with the board's own name rather than executed as a string and found out at run time.
#
# Writing a place is a swap when the slot is taken, so lane goes first and rank second, and the
# order these are called in is the order everybody ends up in.

verb hold(who, l):
  who.lane = l
  who.rank = 0

verb arrive(who, l):
  who.lane = l
  who.rank = 3
